message.content:
{
  "technical_and_design_decisions": [
    "For U1, no changes are required for Node.js because it already passes the transactional context as the first parameter; only the Java contract API needs modification.",
    "For U1, implement a per-transaction instance of the context object in Java to ensure thread safety, rather than using a shared static instance.",
    "For U2/U3, create a new Go package 'protoutils' and move utility/extension code out of 'protos/utils', leaving 'protos' for generated consumable artifacts only.",
    "For U4, backport the Kafka health check functionality from master to the Fabric 1.4 LTS branch, adapting to the older Kafka dependency if necessary.",
    "For U5, introduce an explicit read-only invoke (e.g., Query) that only permits ledger Gets and can be called by channel Readers, instead of dynamically checking ACLs per operation.",
    "For U6, add a new peer configuration option for an external endpoint specifically advertised via service discovery, independent of the gossip bind address.",
    "For U7, add a '/version' endpoint to the existing operations service (HTTP) for both peer and orderer, returning build/version metadata.",
    "For U8, rewrite the Go samples using idiomatic Go patterns (proper error handling, context usage, modules) suitable for beginners."
  ],
  "assumptions": [
    "A single developer with working knowledge of the Hyperledger Fabric codebase will perform all tasks; effort is expressed in person-workdays (8-hour days).",
    "U2 and U3 are identical and are implemented as a single refactoring activity.",
    "The target branch for all changes is Fabric 1.4 LTS unless otherwise specified (U4 explicitly).",
    "Effort estimates include coding, local unit/integration testing, and minor documentation, but exclude independent QA and elapsed calendar time.",
    "Existing CI and build tooling are available; time spent waiting on CI is not counted, but fixing failures is included.",
    "No new third-party dependencies are required for these changes."
  ],
  "activities": [
    {
      "activity_id": "A1",
      "activity_name": "Design Java transactional context API",
      "activity_description": "Design the API to expose transactional context (stub and other APIs) to contract methods in Java, using a per-transaction instance for thread safety. Define interfaces and lifecycle.",
      "most_likely_effort": 3
    },
    {
      "activity_id": "A2",
      "activity_name": "Implement Java transactional context",
      "activity_description": "Implement per-transaction context object creation and wire it into the Java chaincode invocation flow so contract methods can access the stub and APIs safely.",
      "most_likely_effort": 8
    },
    {
      "activity_id": "A3",
      "activity_name": "Test Java transactional context",
      "activity_description": "Write unit and integration tests verifying per-transaction context behavior and thread safety under concurrent invocations.",
      "most_likely_effort": 3
    },
    {
      "activity_id": "A4",
      "activity_name": "Refactor protos/utils to protoutils",
      "activity_description": "Create the protoutils Go package, move utility and extension code from protos/utils, update all imports and build configuration, and verify compilation.",
      "most_likely_effort": 3
    },
    {
      "activity_id": "A5",
      "activity_name": "Backport Kafka health checks to 1.4",
      "activity_description": "Identify Kafka health check commits on master, adapt and backport them to the Fabric 1.4 orderer, ensuring compatibility and adding tests.",
      "most_likely_effort": 4
    },
    {
      "activity_id": "A6",
      "activity_name": "Design read-only invoke for channel Readers",
      "activity_description": "Design an explicit read-only invoke (Query) that only allows ledger Gets, and define access control so channel Readers can invoke it. Specify shim and endorsement changes.",
      "most_likely_effort": 3
    },
    {
      "activity_id": "A7",
      "activity_name": "Implement read-only invoke and ACL changes",
      "activity_description": "Implement the read-only invocation path, enforce no Puts, update ACL checks to permit channel Readers for read-only chaincode, and add tests.",
      "most_likely_effort": 6
    },
    {
      "activity_id": "A8",
      "activity_name": "Add external endpoint config for discovery",
      "activity_description": "Add a new peer configuration option for the external endpoint advertised to SDK users via service discovery, and modify gossip/discovery to use it instead of the bind address.",
      "most_likely_effort": 4
    },
    {
      "activity_id": "A9",
      "activity_name": "Test external endpoint discovery",
      "activity_description": "Write unit and integration tests verifying that service discovery returns the configured external endpoint correctly in containerized environments.",
      "most_likely_effort": 2
    },
    {
      "activity_id": "A10",
      "activity_name": "Add version endpoint to operations service",
      "activity_description": "Implement an HTTP handler in the operations service for peer and orderer that returns version information from build metadata, and add tests.",
      "most_likely_effort": 2
    },
    {
      "activity_id": "A11",
      "activity_name": "Update Go samples to idiomatic style",
      "activity_description": "Review and rewrite existing Go samples to use idiomatic Go expressions and patterns appropriate for beginners and language characteristics.",
      "most_likely_effort": 5
    },
    {
      "activity_id": "A12",
      "activity_name": "Final integration, build, and documentation",
      "activity_description": "Perform full build and cross-component integration of all changes, write/review necessary documentation and release notes, and fix discovered issues.",
      "most_likely_effort": 4
    }
  ],
  "reported_total": {
    "most_likely_effort": 47
  }
}

